A decadent Olive Garden-style baked pasta combining velvety homemade garlic alfredo sauce, savory browned Italian sausage, marinara, and five melted cheeses under a crispy Parmesan-panko crust.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a25241416/five-cheese-ziti-al-forno-olive-garden-copycat/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 lb. sweet Italian sausage
- 1 lb. ziti pasta
- 4 tablespoons butter
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- 4 tablespoons all-purpose flour
- 2 cups half-and-half
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- Pinch of red pepper flakes (optional)
- 1 cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese, divided
- 3 cups marinara sauce
- 2 cups shredded mozzarella cheese, divided
- ½ cup shredded fontina cheese
- ½ cup grated romano cheese
- ½ cup ricotta cheese
- ½ cup panko breadcrumbs
- Freshly chopped parsley, for garnish

## Instructions

1. **Brown the Sausage:** In a large skillet over medium heat, cook the sweet Italian sausage, breaking it apart with a spoon until completely browned and no longer pink (about 6 to 8 minutes). Drain off excess grease and set aside.
2. **Boil Pasta and Prep Dish:** Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C). Grease a 9x13-inch baking dish with olive oil or cooking spray. In a large pot of boiling salted water, cook ziti until just al dente. Drain and set aside.
3. **Make the Alfredo Sauce:** In a large, high-sided skillet over medium heat, melt the butter. Add the minced garlic and sauté until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in the flour and cook for 1 minute until bubbling and light golden. Slowly stream in the half-and-half while whisking constantly to prevent lumps. Bring to a gentle simmer, stir in ½ cup of the grated Parmesan, and cook for 2 to 3 minutes until thickened. Season to taste with salt, black pepper, and optional red pepper flakes.
4. **Combine Sauce, Sausage, Cheeses, and Pasta:** Remove the alfredo from heat. Stir in the marinara sauce, browned sausage, 1 cup of the shredded mozzarella, the fontina, romano, and ricotta cheeses until creamy and melted. Add the drained ziti and toss until thoroughly coated.
5. **Assemble and Top:** Pour the mixture into the prepared baking dish. Top with the remaining 1 cup of mozzarella. In a small bowl, toss the panko breadcrumbs with the remaining ½ cup of Parmesan, then scatter evenly across the top.
6. **Bake:** Bake uncovered at 375°F for 25 to 30 minutes until bubbling vigorously around the edges and golden brown on top.
7. **Garnish and Serve:** Let rest for 5 to 10 minutes to set slightly before serving. Garnish with chopped fresh parsley.

## Notes

- **Make-ahead:** You can assemble the entire dish ahead of time, cover tightly with foil, and refrigerate for up to 24 hours. When ready to bake, add 10–15 minutes to the covered baking time before uncovering to brown the topping.
- **Cheese substitutions:** Provolone or Asiago make great substitutes if Fontina or Romano are hard to find.
